<title>THAILAND: Grain discharges at Thai ports.</title>
<headline>Grain discharges at Thai ports.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following ships were discharging grain or announced at Thai ports, according to independent surveyors.</p>
<p>    Vessel	    Arrival	 Commodity	  Quantity</p>
<p>(tns) Wadi Alkamar 10/10/96 ARG soymeal 26,900</p>
<p>				    BRZ  soymeal		   8,624</p>
<p>Lady of Lorne  10/10/96     IND groundnut meal	   7,700</p>
<p>				    IND sunflower meal	   1,981</p>
<p>				    IND yellow soymeal	     719</p>
<p>Hanjin Jedda   20/10/96     Australian wheat grain    22,000</p>
<p>Kapitan Anistratenko 21/10/96  IND groundnut meal	  600.2</p>
<p>				    IND rapeseed meal	    2,997.2</p>
<p>				    IND sunflower meal	   5,980</p>
<p>Manisamut Naree 26/10/96    Chilean fishmeal	     3,700</p>
<p>Li Yang	   30/10/96    IND groundnut neal	   4,567</p>
<p>				    IND sunflower meal	   1,538</p>
<p>				    IND yellow soymeal	   1,761.2</p>
<p>Cedar Fortune   27/10/96    U.S. corn gluten meal     10,500</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
